                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "On the surface this game is amazing. There's not much to really complain about with the game itself. It's basic sure, but serviceable. \n\nEnemies are fun to kill. It's fun collecting their dropped items and gold. It's fun watching the enemies pick up and use your own gear against you. It's a grand time.\n\nHowever, all fun dies the moment you meet the online part of this game. The other players are unbearable. Which is hilarious because it's the same dozen people over and over again. Look at the player count, there's only 20 people who play this game consistently. Yet, they fuck you at every turn. \n\nAnyone at any time can murder you whenever and however they choose. And there's no penalties for engaging in it. Which sounds interesting until you think about it for a moment. Anyone, regardless of progression, can engage with someone else in PvP whenever they want. This has lead to high leveled players endlessly killing anyone below them for shits and giggles. Once you die you drop all your gear and inventory. You literally can't fight back.\n\nIf this game didn't have such a gruesome PvP implementation this game could have flourished. If there was a way to play in local single player or on a friends only server this game could have flourished. If they had done literally anything about the PvP problem this game could've been great. \n\nHell, this game could've had a really interesting community if we were allowed to host our own servers and mod the game. I bet a lot of people would love nothing more than to play a simple MMO that's basic in every sense of the word but can be modded to be as complex as you wanted. A lot of people could have had a great start in game design and programing modding a game like this in their free time. This game runs on a potato, it's so accessible that I'm upset you can't.",
